From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Fri, 23 Jan 2026 15:46:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tap-ctl: fix memory leak in tap-ct list

If tapdisk PID is not found, temporary structure must be freed.
Not a big deal, except when enabling Address Sanitizer during tests.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
---
 control/tap-ctl-list.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/control/tap-ctl-list.c b/control/tap-ctl-list.c
index b34aa1dc..0c9d0ecf 100644
--- a/control/tap-ctl-list.c
+++ b/control/tap-ctl-list.c
@@ -379,9 +379,10 @@ tap_ctl_list_pid(pid_t pid, struct list_head *list)
 	}
 
 	err = _tap_ctl_list_tapdisk(t->pid, list);
-
 	if (err || list_empty(list))
 		list_add_tail(&t->entry, list);
+	else
+		_tap_list_free(t);
 
 	return 0;
 }
